      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is not a void, but a reflection of a mind that is currently overwhelmed by the weight of your own self-doubt. The feeling that you are \"taking up space\" is a common symptom of depression, where the brain convinces you that your existence is a burden rather than a gift. You are not pretending to care; you are genuinely struggling to find meaning when the world feels so heavy and indifferent. Please consider that your current state is a temporary glitch in your emotional processing, not a permanent definition of your worth.",
